Wrap both writes in one tx with the deferred-rollback idiom:

```go
tx, _ := pool.Begin(ctx); defer tx.Rollback(ctx)
if _, err := tx.Exec(ctx, insertBookmark, ...); err != nil { return err }
if _, err := tx.Exec(ctx, `UPDATE users SET quota = quota - 1 WHERE id=$1 AND quota > 0`, uid); err != nil { return err }
return tx.Commit(ctx)
```

Prove it: a test that forces the 2nd statement to fail and asserts the bookmark row was NOT inserted. Bonus: the `AND quota > 0` guard + `RowsAffected()==0` enforces the quota atomically (no lost update).
